  "prompt": "We're a four-doctor clinic opening a new premises. I need the network designed with clear separation, because patient information must not be reachable from waiting areas.\n\n- Reception and admin PCs (about 6) handle bookings and records.\n- Consulting rooms have a wired PC each (4 rooms).\n- The waiting area has a shared kiosk PC (1) that patients can use.\n- Patient/consulting traffic must be separate from the waiting area.\n- The records server hosts the clinic's HTTP page and DNS, so it gets a fixed address; everything else is automatic addressing.\n\nWe have a WAN handoff from the ISP for internet. We're not doing patient WiFi yet, so the kiosk stays wired for now.",
